    "code_invariance": "NOT MEASURED \u2014 see limitation",
    "limitation": "This harness measures how many REPAIRS a package needs, not how many GUARDS reject it, and for this artifact the two come apart. A single byte-level fault is often visible at several guards: an absent overt_receipt.sig is seen both by the receipt's witness-reference check and by the signed-receipt-required check, and one restoration clears both. Peeling therefore reports one repair where two guards would fire, which is precisely the structure this experiment exists to detect. No code-invariance figure may be derived from these numbers. The preference for repair peeling recorded in DESIGN.md is hereby withdrawn on the evidence of this run; guard-level fault sets require the non-short-circuiting collect mode that design rejected."
  },
